CommitDate: Tue Oct 6 23:11:28 2026 -0500

    feat: S3-ALERT-001 — consecutive-failure alert gate for the S3 backup cron
    
    The DuckBrain S3 unified backup cron is a no_agent silent watchdog: each
    run only reports ITSELF, so the 2026-10-03 outage (S3-GIT-007) stayed
    broken 3+ days with nobody watching for consecutive failures. This adds
    a stateful gate that counts them across runs.
    
    scripts/s3/s3-alert-gate.sh (new):
    - usage: s3-alert-gate.sh <job-name> <exit-code> [state-dir]
      (default state ~/.hermes/backups/s3-alert-state)
    - exit 0 from the job resets that job's counter; non-zero increments it
    - at S3_ALERT_THRESHOLD (default 3) consecutive failures fires ONE alert
      per crossing; re-alerts every S3_REALERT_EVERY (default 8) failures
      after the first so an ongoing outage never goes quiet forever
    - alert mechanism (chosen after surveying the host): `hermes send` — the
      hermes CLI's script-oriented pipe-to-platform subcommand; no LLM, no
      agent loop, no running gateway needed for bot-token platforms, and its
      exit code makes delivery success observable. On notifier failure a
      clearly formatted ALERT line is appended to the fallback log
      (~/.hermes/backups/s3-alerts.log) and the gate exits 2 so the cron
      record shows the delivery failure. Every alert is logged there as an
      audit trail.
    - S3_ALERT_COMMAND overrides the notifier (tests mock it this way);
      crash-safe state: flock on a dedicated lock file + atomic
      tmp-rename counter writes
    - exit codes: 0 processed, 2 alert fired but delivery failed,
      64 usage error; never masks the caller's own exit code
    
    scripts/s3/duckbrain-s3-unified.sh:
    - calls the gate on BOTH paths via an EXIT trap — exactly one gate call
      per run, success or failure (uses the script's real exit status)
    - TERM/INT signal traps record rc 143/130 so a timeout-killed cron run
      (the native layer's 300s deadline has killed runs before) still
      counts as a failure instead of dying silently before the gate
    - S3_ALERT_GATE=0 disables the gate (tests / one-off manual runs)
    - per-component last-error lines captured for the alert message
    - SKIP (lock contention) exits before any trap is armed: no gate call
    
    scripts/s3/test-alert-gate.sh (new): hermetic harness (mktemp-only,
    mock notifier, stub layers — no real S3/Telegram), 47 assertions:
    threshold/reset cadence, re-alert-at-11 arithmetic, fallback + exit 2,
    per-job isolation, 8-way concurrent counter integrity, env knobs,
    real-wrapper wiring both paths, SKIP-arm no-gate-call, and the
    SIGTERM/timeout path (trap records the kill through the gate).
    
    Verification: 47/47 PASS; RED-proven (wrapper reverted -> 10 wiring
    FAILs; gate removed -> preflight exit 2; never-alert mutation -> 19
    FAILs); shellcheck -S warning clean on all three scripts; existing
    harnesses still green (test-fd-inheritance 14/14, test-push-backoff
    85/85 — both drive the real wrapper).
    
    Addresses S3-ALERT-001.
    
    Co-authored-by: Alexis Okuwa <wojonstech@gmail.com>
